From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: sound: apple,s8000-mca: Add the S8000 CS42L71
 link

The iPhone 6s and 6s Plus headset codec sits on MCA0: consumer I2S, four
16-bit slots, SmartIO FIFO 0x180 / trigger 0xc0, from the ADT's
mca0/audio-codec. apple,s8000-mca is the iPad 5's CS42L81 link (two
slots, a larger FIFO). Add apple,s8000-mca-cs42l71 for this one.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/apple,s8000-mca.yaml | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/apple,s8000-mca.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/apple,s8000-mca.yaml
index 935a8523d..c71cs42l71 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/apple,s8000-mca.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/apple,s8000-mca.yaml
@@ -20,7 +20,9 @@ description: |
   speaker link (TDM), apple,t8010-mca-i2s the playback-only stereo I2S link
   to the headphone codec. apple,s8000-mca-tdm is an A9 MCA driving its own
   clocks from an AP NCO channel, the playback-only speaker link (TDM) of the
-  iPhone 6s Plus. The MCAs are the same block; the compatible names
+  iPhone 6s and 6s Plus. apple,s8000-mca-cs42l71 is their headset I2S link
+  to the CS42L71, which provides the bit and frame clocks. The MCAs are
+  the same block; the compatible names
   the link setup iOS programs into it. The T7001 (A8X) MCA is the older
   "mca-version 1" register layout with the same fields: apple,t7001-mca is
   the playback-only speaker link (TDM) of the iPad Air 2, clocked from an AP
@@ -66,6 +68,7 @@ properties:
     enum:
       - apple,s5l8960x-mca
       - apple,s5l8960x-mca-tdm
       - apple,s8000-mca
+      - apple,s8000-mca-cs42l71
       - apple,s8000-mca-tdm
       - apple,t7001-mca
